1
00:03:36,428 --> 00:03:42,428
Find the ninja within ya.

2
00:07:12,857 --> 00:07:18,857
The Lego Ninjago Movie is a family, comedy,
adventure film directed by Charlie Bean.

3
00:10:49,285 --> 00:10:55,285
Six young ninjas are tasked with defending their island home of Ninjago.

4
00:14:25,714 --> 00:14:31,714
By night, they’re gifted warriors using their skill and awesome
fleet of vehicles to fight villains and monsters.

5
00:18:02,142 --> 00:18:08,142
By day, they’re ordinary teens struggling against
their greatest enemy....high school.

6
00:21:38,571 --> 00:21:44,571
Lloyd (voice), played by Dave Franco.

7
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Garmadon (voice), played by Justin Theroux.

8
00:28:51,428 --> 00:28:57,428
Cole (voice), played by Fred Armisen.

9
00:32:27,857 --> 00:32:33,857
Nya (voice), played by Abbi Jacobson.

10
00:36:04,285 --> 00:36:10,285
Koko (voice), played by Olivia Munn.

11
00:39:40,714 --> 00:39:46,714
Jay (voice), played by Kumail Nanjiani.

12
00:43:17,142 --> 00:43:23,142
The Lego Ninjago Movie is a 2017 animated martial arts comedy film, based on the
toy/kit line of the same name and the TV show starring the same characters.

13
00:46:53,571 --> 00:46:59,571
Directed by Charlie Bean, Paul Fisher, and Bob Logan (in their feature directorial debuts) from a screenplay by Logan, Fisher, William Wheeler, Tom Wheeler, Jared Stern, and John
Whittington, it is the first theatrical film to be based on an original Lego property and the third installment in The Lego Movie franchise as well as its second spin-off.

14
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
The film stars the voices of Dave Franco, Michael Peña, Kumail Nanjiani, Abbi Jacobson, Zach Woods, Fred Armisen, Justin
Theroux and Olivia Munn, as well as a live-action role by Jackie Chan (who also voiced Wu in the film).

15
00:54:06,428 --> 00:54:12,428
The film focuses on a teenage ninja Lloyd Garmadon, as he attempts to accept the truth about his sinister father and
learn what it truly means to be a ninja warrior as a new threat emerges to endanger his homeland.

16
00:57:42,857 --> 00:57:48,857
An animated feature film based on Ninjago was announced in September 2013 by Warner Bros., with The Hageman Brothers writing the
adaptation while Bean was hired to direct the film with Phil Lord and Christopher Miller, Dan Lin and Roy Lee producing.

17
01:01:19,285 --> 01:01:25,285
By May 2014, following the success of The Lego Movie, Warner Bros.

18
01:04:55,714 --> 01:05:01,714
announced that the film would be originally released in September 2016,
which later changed to September 2017 in April 2015.

19
01:08:32,142 --> 01:08:38,142
The cast were signed in to voice the characters in 2016, from June to August.

20
01:12:08,571 --> 01:12:14,571
As with The Lego Movie and The Lego Batman Movie, the
animation was provided by Animal Logic.

21
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
Mark Mothersbaugh, who composed The Lego Movie, composed the film's musical score,
with several artists performing new original songs for the film.

22
01:19:21,428 --> 01:19:27,428
A collaboration between production houses from the United States and
Denmark, The Lego Ninjago Movie was released by Warner Bros.

23
01:22:57,857 --> 01:23:03,857
Pictures in the United States on 22 September 2017.

24
01:26:34,285 --> 01:26:40,285
The film received mixed reviews from critics and was the franchise's first box-office
disappointment, grossing only $123.1 million worldwide against its $70 million budget.

25
01:30:10,714 --> 01:30:16,714
A live-action reboot from Universal Pictures is in development.

26
01:33:47,142 --> 01:33:53,142
The film explores themes of high school, martial arts,
secret identity, ninja, based on toy.

27
01:37:23,571 --> 01:37:29,571
The tone is lighthearted.
